{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_10-13-13-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nR=\\\"4775bba9910d407db571eb0a1cfdf8af\\\"\nupd={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Interpretation of the reproduction receipt \\\"+R+\\\" (completed, exit_code 0) for the wedge investigation. Parsed events: indices 0, 1 and 2 are the control case before the heal, in the observation window and after the fault window, and indices 3, 4 and 5 are the same three phases of the injected-store-error case; the remaining events belong to the older transfer tests that share the harness file. The predicate evaluated is whether the reported outcome reproduces under a different schedule, and it holds: the faulted case shows the same truncated store, stale certificate, single store attempt and stalled commit, while the control converges. The defect claim is unchanged and stays asserted; this receipt is a second, independent run of the same fixed experiment.\\\",\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"0bfc2ea5a9e94316982943d306eefbf6-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"82c1d0635aa84b74a3777ab86bb5dcee-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"appendentries-conflict-truncate-block\\\",\\\"appendentries-store-failure-todo\\\",\\\"appendentries-entry-loop-cached-lastlog\\\",\\\"replication-nextindex-floor\\\",\\\"inmem-store-getlog-missing\\\",\\\"state-getlastentry\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{R:[3,4,5,0,1,2],\\\"2086b09f107d4d49b1407754feabb781\\\":[3,4,5,0,1]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"holds\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"bbd3f51dd21745fb821f9adb6ea7d352-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"One allowed StoreLogs error after a conflicting-suffix deletion leaves the follower unable to converge, and removing the error does not restore progress.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"b7e0a0828e794c5fa40df351cb813d8f-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The entry loop returns on a GetLog error for entries at or below the cached last index, before reaching StoreLogs.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Faulted case in the fresh run (indices 3, 4, 5): after the heal the observation window shows the certificate fixed at (4,2) in every sample while the store's last index moves from 4 down to 2, the StoreLogs attempt counter rises only once (from 2 to 3), GetLog of the certificate index reports 'log not found', and commit and applied stay at 2; the post-window sample is unchanged, so the replica is still wedged exactly as in the original receipt. Control in the same run (indices 0, 1, 2): the certificate moves from (4,2) to (5,3), the store's last index from 4 to 5, the attempt counter from 2 to 4, GetLog of the certificate index succeeds and commit reaches 5, so the same legal history converges when the single store error is absent. The two runs used separate clean copies of the same fixed harness with the same inputs, and the scheduling differs: node identities are regenerated and the reject/retry rounds, election timings and transport round trips are independent. Interpretation: the predicate 'the reported outcome reproduces under a different schedule' holds for the four elements that matter to the finding - the truncated durable log, the stale certificate, the absence of any further store attempt, and the stalled commit - and the control still converges in the same run, so the earlier account is not an artefact of one schedule. This is a reproduction, not universal confirmation: it is one repeat of one fixed experiment, and the mechanism remains the source-visible one already recorded.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"A reproduction with the same injected fault still depends on the same staging construction, so it shows schedule robustness rather than independence from the harness.\\\",\n   \\\"This repeat of the core experiment does not exercise the escalation and repair phases; those live in the later receipts, and their own outcomes are unchanged.\\\",\n   \\\"The control and faulted cases in this run are separate cluster instances, as in the original, so the comparison remains between equivalent configurations rather than one instance.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"One additional run of one fixed experiment in a single process with the in-memory transport and the same timeouts; 'reproduces' is scoped to that.\\\",\n   \\\"The observation windows are the ones the fixed harness defines (1500 ms plus a post-window sample), and no longer-run behaviour is claimed.\\\",\n   \\\"The commit stall in this repeat is visible as the unchanged commit index at the post-window sample; the client-future observation belongs to the later escalation receipts.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"Both receipts belong to the same fixed experiment: the earlier one is its first run and this one is the repeat requested from the retained inputs, executed from a separate clean copy with identical inputs. They are not fragments of one history; each is a complete run of the same harness, and this interpretation cites both only to state that the outcome recurred.\\\",\n  \\\"report_title\\\":\\\"卡死副本的核心结果在独立调度下复现\\\",\n  \\\"report_answer\\\":\\\"对核心实验（固定实验 82c1d0635aa84b74a3777ab86bb5dcee）从保留输入再做一次干净复现，保留执行 \\\"+R+\\\" 得到与首次一致的结果：注入一次合法 StoreLogs 错误后，该跟随者的存储最后下标由 4 降到 2、缓存证书整个窗口固定为 (4,2)、GetLog 报 log not found、StoreLogs 尝试次数仅由 2 增到 3、commit/applied 停在 2，窗口后采样仍无变化；同一执行中未注入错误的对照组则收敛（证书 (4,2)→(5,3)、存储 4→5、尝试次数 2→4、commit 5）。由于两次运行使用独立干净副本与重新生成的节点标识，调度、选举时点与传输往返互不相关，说明前述账户不是单一调度的产物。这是复现而非普遍性证明：仅为同一固定实验的一次重复，机制仍以此前记录的有源说明为准。\\\"\n }]\n}\nopen('update.json','w').write(json.dumps(upd,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nprint('ok', json.load(open('update.json'))['interpretations'][0]['conclusion'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
